# Local development only. Copy to .env — never commit the real file.
#
# In AWS none of these are set. Lambda receives SSM parameter *paths* and
# resolves the values at runtime, so secrets never touch Terraform state, and
# backend/src/lib/secrets.ts prefers these direct env vars when present.
#
# The deployed bot has no Anthropic key at all: the parser authenticates by
# workload identity federation, minting an AWS-signed JWT from its own IAM role
# and exchanging it for a short-lived token. See backend/src/lib/anthropic.ts.

# The one place a key is still needed. scripts/parse.ts runs on a laptop with
# no IAM role to federate from, so anthropic.ts falls back to this when set.
# Lambda never sets it.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Override the receipt-parsing model. Defaults to claude-sonnet-5.
# VISION_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# Only needed if you run the bot locally against a tunnel.
# BOT_TOKEN=123456:ABC-DEF...
# WEBHOOK_SECRET=generate-with-openssl-rand-hex-16
